1
00:00:05,778 --> 00:00:08,197
Whiskers and the City of Lights.

2
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:24,275
Ever since the Moon Fish, Whiskers had napped on the windowsill every day.

3
00:00:28,808 --> 00:00:32,065
Mmf! Who is throwing paper at a sleeping cat?

4
00:00:32,265 --> 00:00:35,157
A postcard from Paris! Look, the Eiffel Tower!

5
00:00:35,357 --> 00:00:39,239
Every night, it sparkles like a thousand stars. Let's go and see it!

6
00:00:39,439 --> 00:00:42,137
Paris... isn't that where croissants come from?

7
00:00:42,337 --> 00:00:45,948
Paris is very far. And my legs are very short.

8
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:53,240
Then we'll ride in that basket. It's going to Paris on the train!

9
00:00:59,218 --> 00:01:04,159
So two cats hid in a picnic basket, and rode the train to Paris.

10
00:01:13,386 --> 00:01:16,507
This basket smells like cheese. I love it.

11
00:01:19,596 --> 00:01:21,410
Psst! Save some cheese for me!

12
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:23,093
Pip! What are you doing here?

13
00:01:23,293 --> 00:01:25,721
Every big adventure needs a brave mouse!

14
00:01:38,198 --> 00:01:43,245
Paris! The City of Lights. Rooftops, bridges, and fresh bread everywhere.

15
00:01:46,334 --> 00:01:49,564
Bonjour, little travellers! You look a little bit lost.

16
00:01:49,764 --> 00:01:51,893
We came to see the Eiffel Tower sparkle!

17
00:01:52,093 --> 00:01:57,214
I am Colette. The tower sparkles at nine tonight. Until then, I show you Paris!

18
00:01:57,414 --> 00:01:59,326
Does your city have croissants?

19
00:01:59,526 --> 00:02:02,583
Mon ami, it has the best croissants in the world.

20
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:16,006
Whiskers followed his nose into the bakery of Monsieur Gaston.

21
00:02:21,622 --> 00:02:24,927
One for me... one for me... and one more for me.

22
00:02:29,461 --> 00:02:31,729
Hey! Who is stealing my croissants?

23
00:02:37,707 --> 00:02:39,971
Since when do I have a cat statue?

24
00:02:44,504 --> 00:02:45,948
Ah... ah... ACHOO!

25
00:02:46,148 --> 00:02:48,320
Come back here, you flour monster!

26
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:57,329
Vite! To the river! Jump on the boat!

27
00:03:03,306 --> 00:03:06,689
We escaped. I planned that. Completely on purpose.

28
00:03:06,889 --> 00:03:08,871
Whiskers, you are covered in flour!

29
00:03:14,848 --> 00:03:19,137
Look! The Louvre, the biggest museum in the world. And its glass pyramid.

30
00:03:19,337 --> 00:03:21,480
It looks like a giant piece of cheese!

31
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:25,389
I must go home now. Nine o'clock at the tower. Don't be late!

32
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:33,192
But the sun was warm, and a full cat is a sleepy cat.

33
00:03:41,337 --> 00:03:44,186
Whiskers! Wake up! The sun is going down! Where are we?

34
00:03:49,442 --> 00:03:52,453
The tower is this way. Or maybe that way.

35
00:03:52,653 --> 00:03:56,316
We're lost, Whiskers. We came all this way, and now we'll miss it.

36
00:04:00,127 --> 00:04:02,430
Lost, mes amis? Then go up, not around!

37
00:04:02,630 --> 00:04:05,195
From the top of the steps, you can see all of Paris.

38
00:04:10,090 --> 00:04:12,601
So many steps. I'm too tired, Whiskers.

39
00:04:12,801 --> 00:04:17,095
Come on, Luna. If a lazy cat can climb them, so can you.

40
00:04:30,295 --> 00:04:31,925
Is it nine o'clock yet?

41
00:04:45,847 --> 00:04:49,315
Oh, Whiskers. It's the most beautiful thing I have ever seen.

42
00:04:49,515 --> 00:04:53,508
I saved something too. The best croissant in Paris. For you.

43
00:04:53,708 --> 00:04:55,528
You saved a croissant? You?

44
00:04:55,728 --> 00:04:57,448
Completely on purpose.

45
00:05:02,703 --> 00:05:08,583
High above Paris, three friends shared one croissant. It tasted better than a hundred.

46
00:05:18,171 --> 00:05:21,152
The picnic basket brought them home again.

47
00:05:26,407 --> 00:05:28,095
Where shall we go next, Whiskers?

48
00:05:28,295 --> 00:05:30,878
Somewhere with a nap. And croissants.

49
00:05:34,689 --> 00:05:40,356
Because the most beautiful sights in the world are even more beautiful when you share them.

